From 1000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MeizIshanDev <mezan@meshan.dev>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fog-0960: touch: QUP0 SE0 GENI SPI driver for Redmi 10C (fog)

Replace topaz I2C QUP0 SE2 FT5452 driver with QUP0 SE0 GENI SPI driver
for Redmi 10C (SM6225/khaje). Dual-probes Novatek NT36525B and FocalTech SPI.
Configures TLMM WEST pins 0..3 (qup0), reset GPIO 86, and IRQ GPIO 80.
Does not touch GPIO 36 (vibrator motor on fog).
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c | 2000 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 1386 insertions(+), 767 deletions(-)

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1,767 +1,1386 @@
 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * topaz (SM6225): FocalTech FT5452 at 0x38 on QUP0 SE2, IRQ GPIO80, reset
- * GPIO86, AVDD enable GPIO36 (no regulator), values from topaz-woa
- * TopazTouch. Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one
- * thread. Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+ *
+ * Qualcomm SM6225 ("khaje") QUP0 SE0 GENI SPI Touchscreen Driver
+ * for Xiaomi Redmi 10C ("fog") on Apple XNU (xnu-8796 / iOS 16).
+ *
+ * Supports dual-sourced SPI touch controllers on Redmi 10C:
+ *   1. Novatek NT36525B (novatek,NVT-ts-spi)
+ *   2. FocalTech SPI (focaltech,fts)
+ *
+ * Hardware Topology (Redmi 10C / fog):
+ *   - Bus:        QUP0 SE0 GENI SPI (0x04a80000), Chip Select 0, Mode 0
+ *   - Clocks:     GCC (0x01400000), APCS Vote (0x7900c mask 0x07c0),
+ *                 SE0 RCG2 (CMD_RCGR 0x17010, CFG_RCGR 0x17014 = 1u, CBCR 0x17004)
+ *   - Pins:       TLMM WEST (0x00500000)
+ *                 GPIO 0 (MOSI), GPIO 1 (MISO), GPIO 2 (CS0), GPIO 3 (CLK) -> mux 1 (qup0)
+ *                 GPIO 86 (Reset, active-low output)
+ *                 GPIO 80 (IRQ, active-low input with pull-up)
+ *   - Note:       GPIO 36 is the ERM vibrator on fog and MUST NOT be driven.
+ *   - Resolution: 720 x 1650 (@2x iOS userland -> sweet_hid_touch(finger, down, x, y))
  */
+
